RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Initialized the required time-allocation plan and began train-only measurement profiling.
Fast evaluation attempt 1 failed because DuckDB materialized null list values as pandas.NA; category serialization now checks for NumPy list arrays explicitly.
Fast evaluation attempt 2 failed on DuckDB's reserved `day` alias; history and aggregate aliases were renamed to unambiguous identifiers.
Implemented cutoff-safe histories, item/user aggregates, directional transitions, affinity and seasonal popularity, CPU ALS, pinned BGE metadata embeddings with Faiss retrieval, train-only recall gates, 56 rank features, LambdaRank, and the structurally frozen Model A/Model B flow.
Fast registered evaluation passed on attempt 3 with full contract shapes and MAP 0.006450291259627986 from the debug fallback.
The first detached full-build shell PID exited while its child identity was ambiguous; a specific lane-0 process was later terminated after `/proc` verification, while the apparent duplicate was verified as lane 3 and left untouched. The lane-0 build was restarted in a tracked foreground session.
Replaced implicit's exhaustive CPU batch recommendation with a Faiss IVF inner-product search over the same ALS factors; exhaustive scoring of roughly 311k by 506k products would have dominated the runtime despite fast factor fitting.
The first full recall pass spent over five minutes in per-row `numpy.isin`; it was interrupted after preserving both fold artifacts and replaced with a stamped, Numba-compiled recall accumulator over flattened labels.
Full build completed in 2,137.1 seconds. The predetermined gates rejected ALS and semantic sources on both folds, so V/T snapshot construction now skips those heavy blocks while retaining their measured fold artifacts and zero-feature interfaces.
Registered full run `run_0005` scored MAP 0.0011921561650875421. A train-only audit then exposed objective mismatch: LambdaRank reported 0.765010 sampled reachable-group MAP but only 0.0005168 macro MAP on all July seeds, while directional-score RRF achieved 0.018682/0.020790 on January/July; the solution's fallback was activated and the decision cached.
Corrected recent global, brand-group, and category item ordering to use five-star 30/91/365-day counts rather than all-rating window counts; all-rating counts remain available as item features.
Proposed target-weighted directional transitions that retain all later-item pairs but give a fourfold contribution to successors rated five stars; retention is pending both train folds.
Train-only transition comparisons retained five-star-only successors and widened event separation 8 -> 15 -> 30 -> 49, improving January/July MAP from 0.01899/0.02124 to 0.02024/0.02310.
Train-only RRF calibration froze directional rank weight 1.0, directional log-score weight 0.02, affinity weight 2.0, and additive popularity weight 0.0; final fold MAP is 0.02161/0.02367 with popularity preserved for ties/backfill.
Proposed decomposing brand-group affinity from broad leaf-category affinity; brand-only retention is pending both train folds.
Train-only affinity decomposition rejected leaf-category retrieval and retained the five most recent liked brand groups. Brand-only weight 4.0 achieved 0.02452/0.02760 MAP; expanding to ten groups was a sub-0.001 tie and was rejected for simplicity.
Within-brand BGE neighbor evaluation initially failed with Numba `NotImplementedError: float16`; cached cosine scores are now promoted to float32 at load time for the compiled candidate interface.
Within-brand BGE neighbor weights changed train-fold MAP by at most +0.00020/-0.00009, inside the tie band, so the extra runtime state was rejected and removed from inference.
Reworked ranker negatives from source-head-only samples to unique source-stratified rank quantiles plus evenly spread fill candidates, addressing out-of-support scores on the full 600-candidate pool.
Quantile negatives improved all-seed July ranker MAP from 0.000517 to 0.002620 but remained far below the 0.027598 RRF and required 249 trees; the supervised ranker remains rejected.
Registered target-aligned run `run_0010` scored MAP 0.02199886628189363; registered brand-only affinity run `run_0011` scored precision 0.010093859400866097, recall 0.05994967189758619, and MAP 0.026771871198458586.
